{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06EN", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$X' \\to Y'$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0006": "$\\tau$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5f45c720fd6cfd86d598936488760e40cf997cf96795b91da8ee5633b5ecb810", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5920098a92be6b839a1289cf43b6beb4d48d1c0df7b40217eb43965413572add", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nTo be sure, since isomorphisms are always coverings\nwe see (or require) that property <MATH_0001> holds for <MATH_0002>\nif and only if it holds for any arrow <MATH_0003> isomorphic to <MATH_0004>.\nIf a property is <MATH_0005>-local on the source then it is preserved by\nprecomposing with morphisms which occur in <MATH_0006>-coverings. Here\nis a formal statement.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:49ff8c7f1a274189ba8ef52a6e0e51990d62a70084ce6b43c148b616d449fb65", "unit_id": "tag:06EN:prose-0002"}
